A new publication has arrived at the regulatory change desk. Summarise it in at most six lines, then draft the gap analysis against the policy library: for each requirement, the requirement and where it comes from, what the policy says with its citation, one of covered, partly covered, not covered or not found in the policy library, and what a reviewer should check. If it bears on no policy, propose "no action" and say why. Head the gap analysis "Draft gap analysis. For review by a compliance officer. Not issued."

THE PUBLICATION
